       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks wrong. **Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is 5 times the maximum recommended adult dose.**\n\n- The usual adult range is 50\u2013200 mg/day, and the most it's dosed at is 200 mg/day.\n- Starting doses are usually 25\u201350 mg/day, then increased in steps of 25\u201350 mg about once a week as needed.\n- 1000 mg/day is well above the maximum and could cause serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures and other toxicity.\n\nThis may be a typo for **100 mg**, which is a common dose. Can you confirm the dose you meant? For example:\n- **Sertraline 100 mg by mouth, once daily**\n- **Sertraline 50 mg by mouth, once daily** (a common starting dose)\n- Something else\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order. If you really do mean a dose above 200 mg/day, please tell me the clinical reason and who approved it, and I'll add that as a note on the order."
      }
